    <!-- 三个关键决策点 -->
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="70" topLeftY="290" width="270" height="28">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="14" bold="true" color="rgba(230,0,18,1)" fontFamily="微软雅黑"><p>为什么混合检索</p></content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="70" topLeftY="322" width="270" height="140">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12.5" color="rgba(70,75,85,1)" fontFamily="微软雅黑" lineSpacing="multiple:1.6">
        <p>向量懂"忘记还款≈逾期"，BM25 抓"年费""取现"这类专有名词，两路互补。</p>
      </content>
    </shape>

    <shape type="text" topLeftX="360" topLeftY="290" width="250" height="28">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="14" bold="true" color="rgba(230,0,18,1)" fontFamily="微软雅黑"><p>RRF 融合</p></content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="360" topLeftY="322" width="250" height="140">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12.5" color="rgba(70,75,85,1)" fontFamily="微软雅黑" lineSpacing="multiple:1.6">
        <p>两路分数量纲不同，用倒数排名融合 k=60，无需调权、鲁棒性好。</p>
      </content>
    </shape>

    <shape type="text" topLeftX="630" topLeftY="290" width="270" height="28">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="14" bold="true" color="rgba(230,0,18,1)" fontFamily="微软雅黑"><p>Rerank 为什么必要</p></content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="630" topLeftY="322" width="270" height="140">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12.5" color="rgba(70,75,85,1)" fontFamily="微软雅黑" lineSpacing="multiple:1.6">
        <p>粗排只看"可能相关"，精排模型逐对判断 query 与文档相关性，比直接用 LLM 排序更快更准。</p>
      </content>
    </shape>

    <shape type="text" topLeftX="70" topLeftY="480" width="820" height="25">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="11.5" color="rgba(140,145,155,1)" fontFamily="微软雅黑">
        <p>双栈：本地 BGE-small-zh + bge-reranker-base ｜ 在线 text-embedding-v3 + gte-rerank-v2 ｜ 生成统一 qwen-plus</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
  </data>
  <note><content textType="body"><p>这是技术核心页。</p><p>整体是两段式：先粗排召回10个候选，再用Rerank精排取4个。</p><p>为什么混合：向量懂语义但不懂专有名词，BM25相反，两路互补。</p><p>RRF是融合公式，k=60是论文默认值。</p><p>Rerank是单独一步，把粗排结果精排，这是效果提升的关键。</p></content></note>
